      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please stop taking magnesium until you can see your doctor, as even a \"standard\" 400–500mg dose can be dangerous enough to cause kidney failure or heart arrhythmias in someone with stage 3 CKD. Your doctor specifically booked you for a reason because they need to check your current blood levels to ensure your kidneys are strong enough to handle *any* additional magnesium load. Waiting linearly with sleeplessness is risky; in the meantime, ask your doctor or pharmacist if a non-supplement remedy like magnesia kernels, castor oil packs, gentle stretches, or specific electrolyte mixes are safe for you to try tonight.",
